ROLE: systems_reviewer  VOTE: red
PROMPT_VERSION: v001
EXISTING_IMPLEMENTATIONS: [
  {system: "vLLM Automatic Prefix Caching", url: "https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/design/prefix_caching/", overlap: "Shipping exact-prefix/block-hash KV reuse baseline; hashes each KV block with parent/prefix tokens, so it does not recover schema tokens after the first differing value."},
  {system: "SGLang RadixAttention", url: "https://www.lmsys.org/blog/2024-01-17-sglang/", overlap: "Shipping radix-tree KV reuse for shared prefixes across LLM calls; same baseline class as APC/RadixAttention, not non-prefix schema reuse."},
  {system: "TensorRT-LLM KV cache reuse", url: "https://nvidia.github.io/TensorRT-LLM/advanced/kv-cache-reuse.html", overlap: "Shipping same-prompt/prefix page reuse with block sharing, LRU/offload; cache-management baseline, not schema-after-variable reuse."},
  {system: "TensorRT-LLM priority KV eviction/events", url: "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/introducing-new-kv-cache-reuse-optimizations-in-nvidia-tensorrt-llm/", overlap: "Shipping workload-aware retention for discrete token ranges and KV-aware routing events; improves reuse policy, not a new shifted-position reuse mechanism."},
  {system: "Prompt Cache", url: "https://proceedings.mlsys.org/paper_files/paper/2024/hash/a66caa1703fe34705a4368c3014c1966-Abstract-Conference.html", overlap: "Direct prior art for modular reusable prompt segments; uses schema-defined prompt modules and positional handling to reuse attention states across prompts."},
  {system: "CacheBlend / LMCache", url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.16444", overlap: "Direct prior art for non-prefix KV reuse with selective recomputation/fusion; LMCache README also claims reuse of any reused text, not necessarily prefix: https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache"},
  {system: "FlashInfer", url: "https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer", overlap: "Kernel substrate with paged/ragged KV cache and cascade attention for shared prefixes; low overlap with the proposed cache policy itself."}
]
CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: integration-only
SCALE_REALISM: L0 is not a realistic serving artifact: deterministic word/punct tokenizer, no real RoPE KV tensors, no GPU serving stack, no cache memory pressure, and no real agent trace. As a negative test it is still directionally useful: in the claimed variable-length regime, position-aware reuse is only 0.111-0.189 of tokens, only 26-42% of the token ceiling, and the APC-beyond-prefix gain is 0.051-0.063, below the preregistered 10% threshold. Realistic L1 would need BPE tokenization, real allclose/bytewise KV checks, vLLM/LMCache/Prompt Cache baselines, and H100 cost for re-anchoring versus recompute.
RATIONALE: Red. The systems claim is not a surviving systems insight/design. The packet’s own evidence says the opportunity exists at token level: schema is 42-44% of tokens while exact-prefix captures 6-13%, but the load-bearing systems mechanism fails under position dependence. In the realistic variable-length setting, RoPE position tax is 0.24-0.32 and post-first-value schema reuse is only 3448/23199 = 14.9%, while pre-value schema reuse is exactly the prefix APC already captures. The fixed-length control proves alignment is required, not that the claimed different-value/different-length workload works. Prior art closes the remaining gap: Prompt Cache already defines reusable schema/modules with positional handling, and CacheBlend already targets non-prefix KV reuse via selective recomputation/fusion. Without re-anchoring this is a sub-threshold 5-6% special case; with re-anchoring it collapses to existing Prompt Cache/CacheBlend mechanisms.
